{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/524762-werewolf-teenwolf-how-would-you-do-it","id":524762,"title":"Werewolf + Teenwolf how would you do it?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-22T14:48:23-07:00","id":524762,"title":"Werewolf + Teenwolf how would you do it?","content":"I suspect someW:tA fans do not like the show and that some like it, and some are going &quot;Teen Wolf wtf is that?&quot;.<br /> <br /> It's a TV show for teens/adults on some network in the US. I just watch it and don't think too hard and am able to enjoy it. It has the concept of &quot;Alpha&quot; werewolves who are more powerful than &quot;Betas&quot; and their bite can make new werewolves. Adults who get the bite typically die, and so do children. Teenagers are the ideal candidate to become Betas.<br /> <br /> Rarely, Alphas happen naturally due to a transformation from trials and strength of character. More often, Alphas are killed, and the victor becomes an Alpha. Betas can also be born from other werewolves. In the show, the &quot;transformation&quot; typically is no more than Glabro, with S1 showing more of a Crinos form for the villian.<br /> <br /> How would you fuse this with this with W:tA?<br /> <br /> My initial thoughts are that &quot;bitten&quot; werewolves are very weak, and can only shift into Glabro - and that &quot;born&quot; werewolves can shift into all of the forms. Mechanically Bitten werewolves have 0 Gnosis until they grow in strength somehow. &quot;Alphas&quot; are a result of some kind of transformation or Gift received through a Spirit.<br /> <br /> Thoughts?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2783,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","user":"Tytalus","date":". 10-27-2019, 11:32 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T14:54:41-07:00","id":524781,"title":"","content":"The transmission method is like the rage zombie fomori that Pentex occasionally gets out in W20 Book of the Wyrm.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T15:33:05-07:00","id":524826,"title":"","content":"I probably wouldn't use WtA for this. The amount of stuff I'd need to toss out, rework, and so on, just makes it not worth the effort of using baseline.<br /> <br /> I might consider (somewhat in the vein of what Saur Ops pointed at) using Kami; which are Gaian spirit possessed instead of bane possessed. Whether using the Revised book Possessed, or the current options available in W20 and W20 Umbra the Velvet Shadow, building a Kami is flexible enough it is a lot easier to get towards what you'd want for this.<br /> <br /> Building in custom powers for infectious bites making new ones is simple enough. The passing of Alpha status can be part of the Geasa. Alphas simply get more Kami powers to pick from than Betas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T16:18:33-07:00","id":524899,"title":"","content":"Transmission by bite also makes me think of the Ratkin's Birthing Plague. Random people get bitten, most die. If they are kinfolk through some remote bonds, they have a small chance of survival. What follows is a period of increasing insanity that can last for a long, long time. They begin to have visions, hear voices, etc. The final stage is the full Crinos transformation, when something sends them over the edge. After that, they're officially Ratkin. Maybe you could incorporate parts of that system?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imagizer.imageshack.us/v2/125x125q90/593/w20supporterhiddengarou.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3312-taci","name":"Taci","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3312_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"63"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-22T17:53:54-07:00","id":524953,"title":"","content":"IIRC the Birthing Plague rules are a bit harsher than the Teen Wolf mythos, but that's not really that hard to adjust for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-23T22:36:48-07:00","id":526412,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Taci</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/524762-werewolf-teenwolf-how-would-you-do-it?p=524899#post524899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Transmission by bite also makes me think of the Ratkin's Birthing Plague. Random people get bitten, most die. If they are kinfolk through some remote bonds, they have a small chance of survival. What follows is a period of increasing insanity that can last for a long, long time. They begin to have visions, hear voices, etc. The final stage is the full Crinos transformation, when something sends them over the edge. After that, they're officially Ratkin. Maybe you could incorporate parts of that system?</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this!","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2783-tytalus","name":"Tytalus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2783_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"491"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-24T14:11:49-07:00","id":527046,"title":"","content":"Honestly, W:tA werewolves are so different mechanically from the sort portrayed on <i>Teen Wolf</i> that you'd probably be better off going with another game system entirely. Champions/HERO Games has lycanthropy rules that suit the TV show version pretty well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3505-matt-the-bruins-fan","name":"Matt the Bruins fan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2401"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T14:18:35-07:00","id":594139,"title":"","content":"Please, don't.......never liked this latest series and always preferred the <b>Michael J. Fox</b> version. I think there was even earlier movie version, but never seen it. There were quite few of those.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://scontent-lax3-1.xx.fbcdn.net/hphotos-xfl1/v/t1.0-9/11999058_1477906402511404_6367649438608181692_n.jpg?oh=70d49fe91b2932b397dc24c5df2764ba&amp;oe=56A3338B\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1056-wolf-man","name":"Wolf-Man","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1056_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"145"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-17T16:18:45-07:00","id":594214,"title":"","content":"try forsakens set up, it'll work better.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /> WoD-Dark Eras!! (Backed for Viking Age Werewolf)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1939-lyrics-of-war","name":"Lyrics Of War","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1939_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1769"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-18T10:28:03-07:00","id":594831,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wolf-Man</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/524762-werewolf-teenwolf-how-would-you-do-it?p=594139#post594139\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Please, don't.......never liked this latest series and always preferred the <b>Michael J. Fox</b> version. I think there was even earlier movie version, but never seen it. There were quite few of those.</div> </div> </div> </div>I was a teenage Werewolf, is the older film. Started a young Michael Landon or Pa Ingalls from Little House on the Prairie the tv show.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/293-lncbill","name":"lncbill","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar293_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"523"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-07-19T05:24:43-07:00","id":595547,"title":"","content":"Neco, Necro, Necro, Necro... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:arial\">What doesn't kill you, makes you...<i> stranger</i>.</span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1182-asmodai","name":"Asmodai","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1182_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2989"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}